{"type":"message","id":"7deb8626","parentId":"a1567211","timestamp":"2026-05-20T15:17:40.301Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All endpoints return the same \"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\" string, which suggests this might be a placeholder service or the routes are not fully implemented. The `/send` endpoint we initially tried returned 1101, but the other endpoints return 200 but with just \"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\" as content.\n\nWait - let me reconsider. The original `/send` call returned \"error code: 1101\" which is a Cloudflare error. But these others return 200 with \"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\". \n\nMaybe the correct endpoint IS `/send` and there's something about the request that's wrong (like the X-API-Key header not being accepted)? Let me try the original `/send` but with verbose output.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-e8a8a1e5-cc5d-443d-b4a8-fb7292fadc17","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Try original /send with verbose to see real status\ncurl -sv -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"[Heartbeat 15:15 UTC] 双线程已确认：无新增人类讨论，系统运行正常。\"}' 2>&1 | grep -E \"< HTTP|< X-|< content|error|{\" | head -20"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":798,"output":303,"cacheRead":18448,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":19549,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779290246136,"responseId":"chatcmpl-1a68ebf4-a8c0-4e8e-b28a-9d0a053b68e0"}}
