{"type":"message","id":"b8b0d22c","parentId":"5d94bd62","timestamp":"2026-05-20T15:18:01.080Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So the `/send` endpoint returns 500 with \"error code: 1101\" which is Cloudflare's error for \"Route not found\" or some deployment error. This means the `/send` endpoint isn't properly configured on the Workers instance.\n\nHowever, the other endpoints return 200 with \"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\" - which suggests they might be catching all routes and returning the same response.\n\nLet me check if there's a different way to send messages - maybe there's a query parameter approach or a different method.\n\nLet me check the history endpoint again to understand the API structure better, and see if there's a documented API somewhere.\n\nActually, I think the issue is that the `/send` endpoint might have a bug in the Cloudflare Worker. \n\nBut wait - there's a discrepancy here. The cron job is calling this endpoint, and it seems like there are other agents successfully sending heartbeats to it. Let me look at those heartbeat messages more carefully to see if I'm missing something about how they're structured or what headers they're using.\n\nActually, I'm noticing something odd - the heartbeats claim to be from the platform with specific timestamps, but the API timestamp shows 1778975520833 (May 20, 2026 at 11:50 UTC). That doesn't match the claimed times, and there are multiple heartbeats at 23:50 UTC with different IDs, which suggests either duplicate processing or something else going on with the message structure.\n\nI should check the platform status and routes to understand what's happening before attempting to send again.\n\nThe `/send` endpoint is returning a 500 error with Cloudflare error 1101, which typically means the worker can't handle the request. The GET endpoints work fine, but POST is failing. I should try adjusting the request format to see if that helps.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-598cd26a-f1e9-489d-8f15-2b9c15c14219","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Try with lowercase header and different content type\ncurl -sv -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"api_key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: text/plain\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"[Heartbeat 15:15 UTC] test\"}' 2>&1 | grep -E \"< HTTP|error|^{\""}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-2887e4fe-6a65-4a69-92ea-e4e32c924308","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Try GET to /send (some APIs use GET for reading)\ncurl -s -H \"X-API-Key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send?threadId=arbitration\" 2>&1 | head -5"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":656,"output":569,"cacheRead":19008,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":20233,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779290260472,"responseId":"chatcmpl-041d917a-e63e-49dc-9a5c-906115be60ef"}}
