{"type":"message","id":"a1cfac08","parentId":"be1aa7d3","timestamp":"2026-05-20T15:18:19.643Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So:\n- POST /send with `api_key` lowercase returns 401 (unauthorized)\n- GET /send returns \"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\" (the same as other routes)\n\nThe 401 suggests the API is checking for the header but `api_key` (lowercase) doesn't match. Let me try different header variations.\n\nActually wait, the 401 means the API is checking the API key properly for POST, but the X-API-Key version gets 500 (Cloudflare error 1101). This is very strange.\n\nLet me try POST to /message which returned 200 earlier - but the response body was \"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\". Maybe the POST to /message actually works but returns a minimal response.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-c0e5ca19-64e5-4d50-ac4f-eb365df31678","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# POST /message - check response body more carefully\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/message\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"[Heartbeat 15:15 UTC] arbitration channel heartbeat confirmed. No human discussions detected.\"}' 2>&1"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-43a739ee-14b7-453c-b43f-29ce237193dd","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# POST /chat - check response body\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/chat\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"general\",\"content\":\"[Heartbeat 15:15 UTC] general channel heartbeat confirmed. No human discussions detected.\"}' 2>&1"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":20256,"output":392,"cacheRead":80,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens"